--- 4. arithmetic observation (editorial, recorded as an OPEN/deferred NC; not a design issue) ---
the retrieval log's labelled inference states the design-time default load assumption as
"16 777 200 (0xFFF3D8)"; the correct hexadecimal for 16 777 200 is 0xFFFFF0 (0xFFF3D8 = 16 774 104).
Effect on conclusions: NONE. The inference is a labelled hypothetical resting on two unconfirmed
assumptions (default load = the cited driver's maximum; prescaler = 256); the implied counter
clock is ~1.6026 MHz versus ~1.6021 MHz and the reaction-window ceiling ~2.555 ms versus
~2.556 ms, i.e. the same "~1.6 MHz" and "~2.6 ms" figures. The value is NOT adopted anywhere:
it appears only in the log's labelled-inference block and in the body as "a labelled inference,
not a value". The specification body itself uses the correct form (decimal 16 777 200; 0xFFFFF0
in F-16). Registered as NC-EXT-206 (OPEN, deferred). The frozen retrieval log was NOT edited.

